Z||000000||Black86SE||12-11-2001||11:18 AM||||I was wondering if anybody knew of a good rebuild kit for the 2.8? I don't need pistons though cause mine are fine. I am looking for one that comes with rings, seals, complete gasket set, bearings, and timing stuff. I have found a bunch of kits but I wondered what you people who have rebuilt you engines used. Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Black86SEsig_1.gif">  <BR>Black 1986 SE V6<BR>Automatic - 5-speed soon!<BR>17" Motegi MR7 Wheels<BR>P235/45/ZR17 <BR>BF Goodrich g-Force KDWS<BR>AIM ScreenName: Black86se||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||12-11-2001||11:26 AM||||I just used NAPA parts, wasn't <I>too</I> expensive. (New head gaskets, rods, seals, everything on the top half.) However, I ended up with bad knocking and no oil pressure about six months later, so it was a complete waste of time and money.  (Just my experiance.)<P>Why are you rebuilding it?  Did your head gaskets go?  I had so much coolant in my engine, that I'm sure that's what ate away at my lower bearings.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I bought a new 2.8 long block with a 3 year/75000 mi warranty in May.  Wish I had just done that from the begining.||||reg||1
Z||000002||kneebarx||12-11-2001||01:50 PM||||fierostore, no?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Neal||12-11-2001||02:08 PM||||take it to a machine shop and have them prep everything, chances are youll need new pistions b/c they will wear the cylinder bores, and eveything can be checked out.<P>Cheapo shops will get you everything you need parts and labour for a good price.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black86SE||12-11-2001||06:19 PM||||Well, the engine only has 109,000 miles on it but I took it out to do a tranny swap and paint it. I just figured that I would change the rings and bearings as well as the seals so a not to have a leak in the near future. Once I get the engine back in I don't want to have to take it out again. The pistons look very good with only a tiny bit of blow-by. Never got past the oil ring. The timing chain was very loose and has probably never been changed. The cam and lifters seem to be just fine as well as the crankshaft. The cylinder walls have no scoring, but I am gonna hone them before I put everything back in. I also see that some of the rebuild kits also come with an oil pump so I might replace that too.||||reg||1
